ber 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>40\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 50\u00b0F, and the record is 70\u00b0F (2010). The low of <strong>33\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Mansfield has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Mansfield's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Mansfield has set <strong class=\"sig\">31 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 91 that chance alone would give, and <strong>101 record highs</strong>, close to the 91 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (93). Mansfield's all-time high is 105\u00b0F, on July 21, 1934.","t_chg":"Mansfield's nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 104 complete years: Mansfield's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.25\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.15 to +0.36), about +2.7\u00b0F since 1917. Mansfield's average high shows no clear change: +0.01\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.10 to +0.12) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.62\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.22 to +1.02) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.74\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.33 to +1.16). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Mansfield has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Mansfield's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.46 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.05 to +0.88), about +5.8 inches since 1900. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 42.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1990 (67.22 in); the driest, 1963 (21.81 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, 1 daily record low"}}